material remain unchanged. In a mixed file, this license covers only the
original contributions not already separately licensed, not the entire file.
Nothing here limits any prior grant, applicable hosting-platform permission,
or right available under law.
The component scope and notices are recorded in
Blitz/setup/licensing/NOTICE.md and docs/license-inventory.csv.

2. Free internal use

Subject to these terms, EauDoon grants you a worldwide, non-exclusive,
royalty-free copyright license to use, reproduce and modify the Covered
Material for your own internal purposes if you are:

(a) an individual acting for your own account; or
(b) a startup with fewer than 100 employees OR a valuation below
    US$50,000,000.

Either startup threshold is sufficient. Both thresholds are strict: exactly
100 employees does not satisfy the employee threshold, and exactly
US$50,000,000 does not satisfy the valuation threshold. An unknown valuation
does not prevent reliance on the employee threshold. An unknown employee
count does not prevent reliance on the valuation threshold.

Use on behalf of an organization is that organization's use. An employee or
other individual cannot use the individual permission to bypass the
organization's eligibility. No age, revenue, funding-stage, profitability or
incorporation requirement is added to the startup thresholds.

Assess eligibility at the time of use in good faith using reasonably available, current
information about the startup and, for valuation, a reasonably supportable
company valuation expressed in US dollars. No public disclosure of private
business information or independent appraisal is required. If neither
threshold can be established, obtain written permission before use. If a
startup satisfies neither alternative, obtain written permission
before continuing internal use. Past use while eligible remains permitted.

